   "end": 151.293,
   "src": "clips/read1-10-27-adbe8a943294.mp3",
   "adr": 0,
   "unread": false,
   "lead": 0.18
  },
  {
   "line": "28",
   "scene": 11,
   "text": "We also need constant confidence that our code matches our intentions.",
   "clip": "audio/read1/11-28.wav",
   "at": 153.27,
   "start": 153.45,
   "end": 157.19,
   "src": "clips/read1-11-28-21c24762de4d.mp3",
   "adr": 0,
   "unread": false,
   "lead": 0.18
  },
  {
   "line": "29",
   "scene": 11,
   "text": "Coherence uses your language server to detect security bypasses. The moment an agent writes code that touches something sensitive without routing through a designated chokepoint, the project goes red.",
   "clip": "audio/adr/20260924-221435-take-rslydvhg/29.wav",
   "at": 157.696,
   "start": 157.876,
   "end": 168.916,
   "src": "clips/20260924-221435-take-rslydvhg-29-8cf80f452746.mp3",
   "adr": 2,
   "unread": false,
   "lead": 0.18
  },
  {
   "line": "30",
   "scene": 12,
   "text": "The agent discovers the violation immediately.",
   "clip": "audio/read1/12-30.wav",
   "at": 168.98,
   "start": 169.15,
   "end": 171.81,
   "src": "clips/read1-12-30-92d318a7d06e.mp3",
   "adr": 0,
   "unread": false,
   "lead": 0.17
  },
  {
   "line": "31",
   "scene": 12,
   "text": "Instead of enforcing security through implicit conventions, we know our intentions are represented in the structure of our projects themselves.",
   "clip": "audio/read1/12-31.wav",
   "at": 172.37,
   "start": 172.55,
   "end": 179.75,
   "src": "clips/read1-12-31-69a6663ff1fe.mp3",
   "adr": 0,
   "unread": false,
   "lead": 0.18
  },
  {
   "line": "32",
   "scene": 13,
   "text": "But how do we check that the agent did what we want?",
   "clip": "audio/read1/13-32.wav",
   "at": 180.12,
   "start": 180.3,
   "end": 182.76,
   "src": "clips/read1-13-32-d5e9ff685193.mp3",
   "adr": 0,
   "unread": false,
   "lead": 0.18
  },
  {
   "line": "33",
   "scene": 13,
   "text": "The Coherence structure view shows you the entrypoints into your project, its major components, and how those components interact with each other. Always accurate and up to date.",
   "clip": "audio/read1/13-33.wav",
   "at": 183.07,
   "start": 183.25,
   "end": 193.45,
   "src": "clips/read1-13-33-b4149fb2c387.mp3",
   "adr": 0,
   "unread": false,
   "lead": 0.18
  },
  {
   "line": "34",
   "scene": 14,
   "text": "When chokepoints are violated, you\u2019ll see it.",
   "clip": "audio/read1/14-34.wav",
   "at": 194.07,
   "start": 194.25,
   "end": 197.09,
   "src": "clips/read1-14-34-eaecfbc4a71d.mp3",
   "adr": 0,
   "unread": false,
   "lead": 0.18
  },
  {
   "line": "35",
   "scene": 14,
   "text": "When a major change alters the relationships between components, you\u2019ll see that too.",
   "clip": "audio/read1/14-35.wav",
   "at": 197.57,
   "start": 197.75,
   "end": 201.87,
   "src": "clips/read1-14-35-a940cafb1780.mp3",
   "adr": 0,
   "unread": false,
   "lead": 0.18
  },
  {
   "line": "36",
   "scene": 14,
   "text": "No more sifting through thousands of lines of code to understand what was built or changed. See your project as it is right now.",
